    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "Silent Spring"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " is one of the most influential science books of the 20th century. In it, American author Rachel Carson focused on the harmful effects of "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "pesticides",
            "zh": "杀虫剂"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " that don’t break down easily. Carson painted a picture of a spring without birdsong. She asked readers to imagine what it would be like to wake up on a morning without these cheerful "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Through her simple and "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "poetic",
            "zh": "富有诗意的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " writing, she made people "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the loss deeply."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "Silent Spring"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " a worldwide movement to protect the Earth. In many places, harmful pesticides like DDT have been "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "banned",
            "zh": "明令禁止"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Some even say Carson "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the course of history. But how much "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " have we really made? More than sixty years after the book’s publication, are our springs full of birdsong, or are they silent?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "A 2019 U.S. study suggests that we still have a long way to go. With "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b6",
            "number": 6
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " exceptions, the results aren’t encouraging. About 29 percent of North American birds—around three billion individuals—have disappeared since 1970. Almost every "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "species",
            "zh": "物种"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " saw a big "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b7",
            "number": 7
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Grasslands were hit hardest, losing more than half of their "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b8",
            "number": 8
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Yet birds are not "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b9",
            "number": 9
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Human activities have caused trouble for countless other animals. Overall, scientists believe that more than a million species are "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b10",
            "number": 10
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Still, the 2019 study offers some "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b11",
            "number": 11
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". U.S. wetlands, "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b12",
            "number": 12
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", are carefully protected by law. There, the number of birds has grown by 13 percent. Raptors, like bald eagles, are another success story. Bald eagles were "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b13",
            "number": 13
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " when Carson wrote "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "Silent Spring"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Today, thanks largely to the DDT ban, their numbers have risen by about 15 million. These exceptions show that our efforts to save the Earth are not completely "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b14",
            "number": 14
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "It won’t be easy, but we must continue "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b15",
            "number": 15
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "—for a spring that is alive and full of birdsong."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
